  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates lotteries based on their maximum and minimum outcomes. It prefers the lottery with the more favorable maximum outcome; if those are equal, it prefers the one with the more favorable minimum outcome. In this case, Lottery A has a maximum outcome of 2500 Euros and a minimum outcome of 0 Euros. Lottery B has a maximum outcome of 2400 Euros and a minimum outcome of 2400 Euros. Therefore, A has a higher maximum outcome (2500 > 2400), and since the maximum outcomes differ, the reason clearly prefers Lottery A over Lottery B. The relevant information for the decision reason is thus available and clearly defined in the lotteries' outcomes and probabilities.",
